---
import PricingCalculator from '../components/PricingCalculator';
import SavedReading from '../components/SavedReading';
import '../styles/global.css';
// Evaluated at build time. Only serializable feature data crosses into React.
const monthlyRate=20;
const features=[['01','Publish the story','Product copy, feature descriptions, and navigation arrive as HTML. Reading them needs no React runtime.'],['02','Add just enough interaction','A calculator receives the seat price and owns its small UI. The rest of the document stays outside that island.'],['03','Give each feature a boundary','Saving a guide is a separate feature with its own state and persistence. Changing seat count does not involve it.']];
const lessons=[['Start with HTML','Disable JavaScript and reload. The story, initial estimate, links, and native FAQ remain readable. The island controls stay disabled.'],['Wake one feature','Re-enable JavaScript. Change seats to 25, then try 0, 1.5, or 1001. Only the calculator updates.'],['Defer another feature','Reload while scrolled to the top. Scroll down to the field note: its save control hydrates when visible. Inspect its directive in index.astro.'],['Choose what persists','Save the guide and refresh. It stays saved on this browser; the calculator returns to its default.'],['Inspect the boundary','Read the React props and state. Neither island mounts the page or shares a React provider with the other.']];
---
<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="UTF-8"/><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width"/><meta name="description" content="An Astro feature-boundary lab: static product content, independent React islands, and a guided learner walkthrough."/><title>Feature Boundary · Astro Lab</title></head><body>
<header><a class="brand" href="#top">◈ Boundary Lab</a><span>ASTRO / FEATURE BOUNDARIES</span><a href="#walkthrough">Follow the lab ↗</a></header>
<main id="top"><section class="hero"><div><span class="eyebrow">CONTENT FIRST. INTERACTION WHERE IT COUNTS.</span><h1>A whole page.<br/><em>A few moving parts.</em></h1><p class="lede">Build a product page people can read immediately. Give the calculator its own browser code. Let everything else remain a document.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="button primary" href="#pricing">Try the feature ↓</a><a href="#boundary">See the boundary ↗</a></div><div class="hero-meta"><span>Static Astro page</span><span>Two React islands</span><span>No database</span></div></div><aside class="map"><div class="map-title">PAGE DELIVERY <span>01</span></div><div class="html-block"><strong>Product story</strong><span>HTML + CSS · built ahead of time</span><div class="mini-lines"><i></i><i></i><i></i></div><div class="mini-island"><span>PRICING CALCULATOR</span><code>client:load</code></div><div class="mini-lines"><i></i><i></i></div><div class="mini-island secondary"><span>SAVED READING</span><code>client:visible</code></div></div><p>Independent features embedded in one readable page.</p></aside></section>
<section id="boundary" class="feature-strip" aria-label="The feature boundary">{features.map(([number,title,body])=><article><span class="number">{number}</span><h2>{title}</h2><p>{body}</p></article>)}</section>
<section id="pricing" class="pricing-section"><div class="section-copy"><span class="eyebrow">FEATURE 01 / IMMEDIATE INTERACTION</span><h2>A small calculator.<br/>A clear responsibility.</h2><p>Imagine this is a team's product landing page. Most visitors read the product story. Some want a quick seat estimate.</p><p>The calculator receives one value from Astro: a monthly seat price. Its React component manages input, validation, and feedback inside that feature.</p><pre><code>&lt;PricingCalculator
  monthlyRate={20}
  client:load
/&gt;</code></pre><noscript><p class="notice">JavaScript is off. The default 10-seat estimate is $200/month; interactive controls are unavailable.</p></noscript></div><PricingCalculator monthlyRate={monthlyRate} client:load /></section>
<section class="native-section"><div><span class="eyebrow">DOCUMENT FEATURES / NO HYDRATION</span><h2>Some interaction is already HTML.</h2><p>These disclosure controls use native browser behavior. They don't need another React island.</p></div><div class="faq"><details><summary>Does this estimate create a subscription?</summary><p>No. It is illustrative math in the browser. A checkout needs a server to validate the actual price, identity, and payment.</p></details><details><summary>Can Astro do more than static pages?</summary><p>Yes. Astro also supports server-rendered routes and server-side features. This lab deliberately uses static output to make the client feature boundary easy to inspect.</p></details><details><summary>Can islands share state?</summary><p>Yes, through an explicit shared store or other communication. Here they don't need to. A large connected workflow may be clearer inside one larger application boundary.</p></details></div></section>
<section id="field-note" class="reading-section"><article><span class="eyebrow">FEATURE 02 / VISIBLE WHEN NEEDED</span><h2>Keep the feature small<br/>until the workflow grows.</h2><p>A product calculator and a saved-reading control answer different questions. Their local state has no reason to travel together.</p><p>When features need a common selection, pending edits, and coordinated recovery, revisit the boundary. The matching Next.js task workspace demonstrates that connected workflow.</p><pre><code>&lt;SavedReading
  articleId="feature-boundary"
  client:visible
/&gt;</code></pre></article><SavedReading articleId="feature-boundary" client:visible /></section>
<section id="walkthrough" class="walkthrough"><div><span class="eyebrow">BUILD WITH THE LEARNER</span><h2>Predict. Try. Inspect.</h2><p>Open the app beside VS Code. Follow a feature from rendered HTML to browser state.</p></div><ol>{lessons.map(([title,body])=><li><h3>{title}</h3><p>{body}</p></li>)}</ol></section>
<section class="resources"><h2>Go deeper at the boundary</h2><a href="https://docs.astro.build/en/concepts/islands/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Astro islands architecture ↗</a><a href="https://docs.astro.build/en/reference/directives-reference/#client-directives" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Choose a hydration directive ↗</a></section>
</main><footer><span>Boundary Lab / Astro feature boundary</span><span>Companion to the Next.js task workspace</span></footer></body></html>
